{
  "schema_version": "1",
  "description": "Hand-checked symbols that the commit range 9bce09b..f33d96c of this repository touched, used by tests/taf_context/test_dogfood_changed.py to measure the precision and the recall of changed-symbols and to cross-check impact-candidates against callers.json. Every entry is a record whose line span at f33d96c meets a changed hunk of its own path: the hunks come from a diff parsed independently of the broker, and the spans from the language's own parser (CPython's ast for Python, go/ast for Go), then every entry was reviewed against the diff by hand. A change inside a method also changes the class that contains it, and a Python definition owns its decorator lines, so nested definitions appear together. Precision and recall are measured over the definition and entry-point findings; module findings are listed separately because a Go module record covers only the package clause, so it is changed only when line 1 is.",
  "range": {
    "base": "9bce09b",
    "head": "f33d96c"
  },
  "restriction": "The range touches 64 paths and 376 symbols, too many to hand-check, so the fixture covers three subtrees: the Python broker package, the Go wire package and the Go extractors. Every one of those paths fits a single query at the largest request settings the CLI accepts (64 results, 12000 characters), which is why the subtree of the change-heavy query package is not part of it: one file added there in the range carries 63 changed symbols and cannot be returned in one answer. The three subtrees change 20 paths, all 20 listed here: 18 carry at least one changed definition, and two (tools/taf-context-native/internal/extract/typescript.go, tools/taf-context/taf_context/state_lifecycle.py) carry an empty changed_symbols list because their only hunk touches no definition (a top-level query-string literal and a module-level constant), so the fixture asserts the engine returns nothing for both.",
